  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For a charged spherical ball, electrostatic potential inside the ball varies with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>.</p><p>Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> are constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the distance from the center. The volume charge density inside the ball is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>&#949;</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is ______.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;permittivity of medium.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>Now, electric field inside the charged sphere is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#949;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;</p><p>Comparing both, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>&#949;</mi></math>.</p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
